{%- comment -%}
  Rewards progress + free gift picker. Rendered in TWO places: the cart drawer
  and the cart page summary. Both surfaces must agree, otherwise a shopper who
  reaches checkout via "View bag" is told a different story from one who uses
  the drawer.

  Markup only. The styles and the click handling live in cart-gift-assets,
  which cart-drawer renders unconditionally - read the comment at the top of
  that file before moving either back in here, because the split fixes a bug
  rather than just tidying.

  Because the cart page also contains the drawer markup, BOTH instances exist
  in the DOM there at once. Nothing here may carry an id or look itself up via
  document.querySelector - it would find whichever copy happens to come first
  and operate on the invisible one. Every lookup is scoped to the enclosing
  [data-gift-block] instead, and the name field uses a wrapping label rather
  than a for/id pair.

  One bar, two milestones: free UK shipping at £20, free gift at £25.

  Colours come from .ship-progress__* - the theme's own classes - rather than
  hardcoded hex, so the bar keeps matching if the palette ever changes.

  Why the picker exists: Shopify's Buy X Get Y discount does NOT put the gift
  in the cart. The shopper has to add it themselves, and only then is it
  discounted to zero. Nothing said so, which is why 22 qualifying orders
  produced exactly one redeemed gift.

  Below the threshold the gifts are still shown, disabled. "Add £2.00 more"
  on its own is an abstraction; seeing the towel you are £2 away from is not.

  gift_threshold must match the 'Free Gift Over £25' AUTOMATIC discount.

  WHAT COUNTS TOWARDS THE £25. Not the gift. Shopify needs £25 of other units
  before it will hand one over, which is why qualifying_total skips the
  free-gifts collection. Verified live:

    £24 of products                      -> no gift
    £24 + one lip balm  (cart £29.95)    -> lip balm still charged
    £24 + two lip balms (cart £35.90)    -> one lip balm free

  The middle row is the one shoppers trip over: the cart clears £25 on paper
  but the only spare unit IS the gift. paid_gift_item spots that case and says
  so rather than leaving them to guess.

  THE DISCOUNT-CODE TRAP. Shopify will not let a Buy X Get Y discount coexist
  with a percentage code, and which one loses depends on the order:

    gift added first, code entered after  -> Shopify refuses the code, loudly
    code active first, gift added after   -> the gift is charged, silently

  The second is the dangerous one. Tested live: with BASKET20 in the session a
  shopper who picked a 'free' lip balm got it at £4.76, no warning anywhere.
  So when a code is already applied the picker is not rendered at all - we
  explain instead. Never offer something the checkout will refuse to honour.

  HOW OPTIONS ARE LAID OUT. The chip row is the scarce space. Measured on an
  iPhone 12 Pro the drawer gives about 300px of usable width, which is two
  chips and no more; a third chip, or a chip with a subtitle, wraps to a
  second row and pushes the checkout button down. So the chip row carries the
  minimum that identifies each gift and nothing else, and every finer
  distinction lives in the panel that opens on tap, which costs no height
  until it is opened.

  The distinction that matters here is kids vs adult. All seven lip balms are
  product_type 'Lip Care', so grouping on type alone offered a parent hunting
  a kids balm Bergamot & Lemon, and offered an adult Kids Strawberry. Two
  separate chips fixed that and cost a chip row. A "kids & adult" subtitle on
  one chip fixed it more cheaply and still wrapped on a real handset. What
  survives is the cheapest version: a bare "Lip Balm" chip whose chevron says
  it opens, onto two labelled rows - Adults, Kids - keyed off the Kids marker
  in the product title. The tags only render when both rows have something in
  them, so if the adult flavours sell out the panel quietly becomes a plain
  list rather than leaving a lone "Kids" tag hanging there.

  That last rule is why the towel's colour row carries NO tag. A row tag earns
  its place by telling two rows apart; with one row there is nothing to tell
  apart, and "Colour" above Green / Beige / White only repeats what the words
  already are. Adding it would also contradict the rule directly above, which
  goes out of its way never to leave a tag standing on its own.

  TWO WAYS A GIFT CAN OFFER A CHOICE, and they look identical to the shopper.
  The lip balms are seven separate PRODUCTS sharing a product_type. The towel
  is one product with three colour VARIANTS. The first version of this picker
  only ever counted products, so a group holding a single product fell to the
  plain-chip branch and added selected_or_first_available_variant without
  asking. Every free towel that went out was Green, and Beige and White were
  unreachable - the stock counts said so plainly, Green draining while the
  other two sat untouched. avail_variant_count is what closes that: a lone
  product with more than one available variant now opens the same panel the
  lip balms use, one button per variant. Both paths end at the same
  data-add-gift / data-variant-id contract, so cart-gift-assets needs no
  change and never learns which kind of choice it just handled.

  Variant buttons additionally carry data-variant-image, which the script uses
  to swap the chip thumbnail to the chosen colour. The three towels are
  genuinely different photographs, so the chip stops being a category icon and
  becomes a preview of the exact bear that will arrive. It falls back to the
  product shot when a variant has no image of its own, and the script ignores
  the attribute entirely when it is absent, which is every lip balm.

  CHIP IMAGES ARE THEIR OWN CROP. The 34px chip renders with object-fit:cover,
  so a product photo composed for a product page arrives here centre-cropped
  and mostly scenery - the bear filled about a third of the disc, the rest was
  a vase and some books. Worse, the three towel photographs are not framed
  alike: the beige shot has a wide ceramic vase crowding the bear where green
  and white have a slim glass one, which made beige read as a smaller bear
  when all three are within 2% of the same height. Measured, not guessed.

  So the variant metafield custom.chip_image holds a square crop centred on
  the subject, normalised so the subject occupies the same fraction of every
  crop. That is the only thing it is for; it is not a second product image.
  It is optional everywhere - both the resting chip and the variant buttons
  resolve it with the same fallback chain, so anything without one drops
  through to the variant image and then the product shot exactly as before.
  Do not point it at a wide photo, and do not reuse it on the product page,
  where the full composition is the point.

  Sold-out variants are skipped, so if Green runs dry the panel simply offers
  Beige and White, and if only one colour is left the chip goes back to being
  a plain one-tap chip rather than opening a panel with a single button in it.

  FLAVOUR NAMES ARE NEVER SHORTENED. A flavour button drops the words the row
  tag and the chip already said - "Lemon", not "Kids Lip Balm Lemon" - and
  nothing else. An earlier version also cut at ' & ', turning "Bergamot &
  Lemon" into "Bergamot", to pull the Adults row back onto one line. That was
  wrong twice over. On a scented product the scent IS the product, so someone
  who dislikes lemon picks it unaware and someone who came for lemon skips it;
  and the rule was general, so a future "Lavender & Chamomile" would silently
  lose its second half with nobody noticing. The row is worth a wrapped line;
  a product name is not worth quietly altering. Padding and gaps were trimmed
  instead. If a longer flavour name ever does wrap, move the row tag onto its
  own line so the buttons get the full panel width - do not cut the name.

  Variant buttons follow the same rule and print the variant title as it is.
  Colour names are short today; nothing here assumes they stay short.

  Nothing is lost by the bare chip either: the flavour count and the full
  product titles live in aria-label, where a screen reader announces them and
  they cost no pixels at all.

  Type sizes here run a step below the theme's own (.72rem chips, .70rem
  flavours) for the same reason - it is what buys the single row. Do not go
  smaller; the flavour buttons are already under a comfortable tap target.

  Anything tagged 'Personalised' collects a name first, mirroring the product
  page exactly - same wording, placeholder, 12-character cap, property name.
  Chip text drops only the word "Personalised"; tapping the chip opens the
  required name field immediately, so the shorter label hides nothing. When
  the item also has variants the colour is chosen first and the name field
  opens after it, because the name panel is what carries the confirm button.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign ship_threshold = 2000 -%}
{%- assign gift_threshold = 2500 -%}
{%- assign qualifying_total = 0 -%}
{%- assign gift_in_cart = false -%}
{%- assign gift_charged = false -%}
{%- assign paid_gift_item = false -%}
{%- assign code_applied = false -%}
{%- assign code_title = '' -%}
{%- assign gift_products = collections['free-gifts'].products -%}

{%- for d in cart.cart_level_discount_applications -%}
  {%- if d.type == 'discount_code' -%}
    {%- assign code_applied = true -%}
    {%- assign code_title = d.title -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{%- for item in cart.items -%}
  {%- for alloc in item.line_level_discount_allocations -%}
    {%- if alloc.discount_application.type == 'discount_code' -%}
      {%- assign code_applied = true -%}
      {%- assign code_title = alloc.discount_application.title -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}

  {%- if item.properties['_free_gift'] and item.final_line_price > 0 -%}
    {%- assign gift_charged = true -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- assign is_gift_product = false -%}
  {%- for gift in gift_products -%}
    {%- if gift.id == item.product_id -%}
      {%- assign is_gift_product = true -%}
      {%- break -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}

  {%- if is_gift_product -%}
    {%- if item.final_line_price == 0 -%}
      {%- assign gift_in_cart = true -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- assign paid_gift_item = true -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- assign qualifying_total = qualifying_total | plus: item.final_line_price -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{%- assign ship_unlocked = false -%}
{%- if cart.total_price >= ship_threshold -%}{%- assign ship_unlocked = true -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- assign gift_unlocked = false -%}
{%- if qualifying_total >= gift_threshold -%}{%- assign gift_unlocked = true -%}{%- endif -%}

{%- assign bar_pct = qualifying_total | times: 100 | divided_by: gift_threshold -%}
{%- if bar_pct > 100 -%}{%- assign bar_pct = 100 -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- assign notch_pct = ship_threshold | times: 100 | divided_by: gift_threshold -%}

<div class="gift-progress" data-gift-block>

  <div class="ship-progress reward-progress">
    {%- if gift_unlocked and code_applied == false -%}
      <p class="ship-progress__msg ship-progress__msg--ok">✓ Free UK shipping and your free gift are unlocked</p>
    {%- elsif ship_unlocked -%}
      <p class="ship-progress__msg ship-progress__msg--ok">✓ Free UK shipping unlocked</p>
      {%- if code_applied == false -%}
        <p class="ship-progress__msg">Add <strong>{{ gift_threshold | minus: qualifying_total | money }}</strong> more for a free gift</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- else -%}
      <p class="ship-progress__msg">Add <strong>{{ ship_threshold | minus: cart.total_price | money }}</strong> more for free UK shipping{% if code_applied == false %}, <strong>{{ gift_threshold | minus: qualifying_total | money }}</strong> for a free gift{% endif %}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="ship-progress__bar reward-bar">
      <span style="width: {{ bar_pct }}%;"></span>
      <i class="reward-bar__notch{% if ship_unlocked %} is-passed{% endif %}" style="left: {{ notch_pct }}%;" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    </div>

    <div class="reward-scale" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="reward-scale__mark{% if ship_unlocked %} is-done{% endif %}" style="left: {{ notch_pct }}%;">{{ ship_threshold | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span>
      <span class="reward-scale__mark reward-scale__mark--end{% if gift_unlocked %} is-done{% endif %}">{{ gift_threshold | money_without_trailing_zeros }} gift</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- if gift_charged -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Shopify charged for the gift. Two different things cause that: a discount
      code cancelled the automatic gift discount, or the basket dropped back
      under the threshold. Naming the wrong one sends the shopper hunting for a
      code they never entered, so each case says what actually happened.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if code_applied -%}
      <p class="gift-alert">Your gift is being charged because {% if code_title != blank %}<strong>{{ code_title }}</strong> is{% else %}a discount code is{% endif %} applied. Remove the code at checkout to get the gift free, or remove the gift from your bag.</p>
    {%- else -%}
      <p class="gift-alert">Your gift is being charged because your basket is now under {{ gift_threshold | money_without_trailing_zeros }}. Add {{ gift_threshold | minus: qualifying_total | money }} more to get it free, or remove the gift from your bag.</p>
    {%- endif -%}

  {%- elsif code_applied -%}
    <p class="gift-progress__note">{% if code_title != blank %}<strong>{{ code_title }}</strong> is applied.{% else %}A discount code is applied.{% endif %} A free gift cannot be combined with a discount code, so no gift is offered on this order. Remove the code at checkout if you would rather claim a free gift.</p>

  {%- elsif gift_in_cart -%}
    <p class="gift-progress__note">One offer per order. If you have a discount code you would rather use, remove the gift from your bag.</p>

  {%- else -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      One chip per product family, in catalogue order. Out-of-stock products
      never form a group, so Cinnamon at zero stock simply vanishes.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign group_names = '' -%}
    {%- for g in gift_products -%}
      {%- unless g.available -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endunless -%}
      {%- assign gl = g.type -%}
      {%- if g.type contains 'Lip' -%}{%- assign gl = 'Lip Balm' -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- assign group_names = group_names | append: gl | append: '||' -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
    {%- assign gift_groups = group_names | split: '||' | uniq -%}

    {%- if gift_unlocked -%}
      <p class="gift-progress__msg gift-progress__msg--ok">Pick your free gift</p>
    {%- else -%}
      <p class="gift-progress__msg gift-locked__title">Your free gift at {{ gift_threshold | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="gift-progress__options{% unless gift_unlocked %} is-locked{% endunless %}">
      {%- for group in gift_groups -%}
        {%- assign avail_count = 0 -%}
        {%- assign first_gift = blank -%}
        {%- for g in gift_products -%}
          {%- unless g.available -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endunless -%}
          {%- assign gl = g.type -%}
          {%- if g.type contains 'Lip' -%}{%- assign gl = 'Lip Balm' -%}{%- endif -%}
          {%- if gl == group -%}
            {%- assign avail_count = avail_count | plus: 1 -%}
            {%- if avail_count == 1 -%}{%- assign first_gift = g -%}{%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          A lone product still offers a choice when it has more than one
          variant in stock - see the note about the towel at the top.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign avail_variant_count = 0 -%}
        {%- if avail_count == 1 -%}
          {%- for v in first_gift.variants -%}
            {%- if v.available -%}{%- assign avail_variant_count = avail_variant_count | plus: 1 -%}{%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          The chip at rest shows the first colour a shopper can actually pick,
          in its own crop where one exists. Resolving it from the first
          AVAILABLE variant rather than from the product's featured image keeps
          the chip honest when a colour sells out: the resting chip is never a
          bear the panel below it cannot offer.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign chip_img = first_gift.featured_image -%}
        {%- if avail_count == 1 and avail_variant_count > 1 -%}
          {%- for v in first_gift.variants -%}
            {%- unless v.available -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endunless -%}
            {%- assign chip_img = v.metafields.custom.chip_image.value | default: v.image | default: first_gift.featured_image -%}
            {%- break -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- assign group_key = group | handleize -%}
        {%- if first_gift != blank -%}
          {%- assign gift_full = first_gift.title | split: '|' | first | remove: 'INCIA ' | strip -%}
          {%- assign gift_label = gift_full | remove: 'Personalised ' | strip -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if avail_count == 1 and avail_variant_count > 1 -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            One product, several colours. Same chip shape as the lip balms so
            the two read as one control, and the same panel opens beneath it.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <button type="button" class="gift-option gift-option--group" {% if gift_unlocked %}data-gift-group="{{ group_key }}" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="{{ gift_full | escape }} - choose from {{ avail_variant_count }} colours"{% else %}disabled aria-disabled="true" aria-label="{{ gift_full | escape }} - {{ avail_variant_count }} colours, unlocks at {{ gift_threshold | money_without_trailing_zeros }}"{% endif %}>
            <img src="{{ chip_img | image_url: width: 96 }}" alt="" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy">
            <span>{{ gift_label }}</span>
            {%- if gift_unlocked -%}
              <svg class="gift-option__chevron" width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 10 10" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 3.5 5 6.5 8 3.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            {%- endif -%}
          </button>

        {%- elsif avail_count == 1 -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            Full title for assistive tech, short label on screen - see the note
            about chip width at the top of this file.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <button type="button" class="gift-option" {% if gift_unlocked %}data-add-gift data-variant-id="{{ first_gift.selected_or_first_available_variant.id }}" data-gift-label="{{ gift_full | escape }}"{% if first_gift.tags contains 'Personalised' %} data-needs-name="Name"{% endif %} aria-label="Add free {{ gift_full | escape }}"{% else %}disabled aria-disabled="true" aria-label="{{ gift_full | escape }} - unlocks at {{ gift_threshold | money_without_trailing_zeros }}"{% endif %}>
            <img src="{{ first_gift.featured_image | image_url: width: 96 }}" alt="" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy">
            <span>{{ gift_label }}</span>
          </button>
        {%- elsif avail_count > 1 -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            Bare label - the chevron says it opens, and the flavour count is in
            aria-label where it costs nothing. See the layout note at the top.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <button type="button" class="gift-option gift-option--group" {% if gift_unlocked %}data-gift-group="{{ group_key }}" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="{{ group | escape }} - choose from {{ avail_count }} flavours"{% else %}disabled aria-disabled="true" aria-label="{{ group | escape }} - {{ avail_count }} flavours, unlocks at {{ gift_threshold | money_without_trailing_zeros }}"{% endif %}>
            <img src="{{ first_gift.featured_image | image_url: width: 96 }}" alt="" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy">
            <span>{{ group }}</span>
            {%- if gift_unlocked -%}
              <svg class="gift-option__chevron" width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 10 10" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 3.5 5 6.5 8 3.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            {%- endif -%}
          </button>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>

    {%- if gift_unlocked -%}
      {%- for group in gift_groups -%}
        {%- assign avail_count = 0 -%}
        {%- assign kids_count = 0 -%}
        {%- assign first_gift = blank -%}
        {%- for g in gift_products -%}
          {%- unless g.available -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endunless -%}
          {%- assign gl = g.type -%}
          {%- if g.type contains 'Lip' -%}{%- assign gl = 'Lip Balm' -%}{%- endif -%}
          {%- if gl == group -%}
            {%- assign avail_count = avail_count | plus: 1 -%}
            {%- if avail_count == 1 -%}{%- assign first_gift = g -%}{%- endif -%}
            {%- if g.title contains 'Kids' -%}{%- assign kids_count = kids_count | plus: 1 -%}{%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
        {%- assign adult_count = avail_count | minus: kids_count -%}

        {%- assign avail_variant_count = 0 -%}
        {%- if avail_count == 1 -%}
          {%- for v in first_gift.variants -%}
            {%- if v.available -%}{%- assign avail_variant_count = avail_variant_count | plus: 1 -%}{%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- assign group_key = group | handleize -%}

        {%- if avail_count == 1 and avail_variant_count > 1 -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            One row, no tag: the chip already said what the product is and the
            only thing left to choose is the variant. Titles print as they are.
            data-variant-image lets the script swap the chip thumbnail to the
            colour being chosen - see the note at the top. It prefers the
            square chip crop and falls back to the variant photo, so the
            thumbnail never changes framing halfway through a choice.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- assign gift_full = first_gift.title | split: '|' | first | remove: 'INCIA ' | strip -%}
          <div class="gift-flavours" data-gift-group-panel="{{ group_key }}" hidden>
            <div class="gift-flavours__row">
              {%- for v in first_gift.variants -%}
                {%- unless v.available -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endunless -%}
                <button type="button" class="gift-flavour" data-add-gift data-variant-id="{{ v.id }}" data-variant-image="{{ v.metafields.custom.chip_image.value | default: v.image | default: first_gift.featured_image | image_url: width: 96 }}" data-gift-label="{{ gift_full | append: ' - ' | append: v.title | escape }}" {% if first_gift.tags contains 'Personalised' %}data-needs-name="Name"{% endif %} aria-label="Add free {{ gift_full | escape }} in {{ v.title | escape }}">{{ v.title }}</button>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </div>
          </div>

        {%- elsif avail_count > 1 -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            Two labelled rows only when both actually have something in them.
            If the adult flavours sell out this collapses back to one unlabelled
            row rather than leaving a lone "Kids" tag hanging there.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- assign show_tags = false -%}
          {%- if kids_count > 0 and adult_count > 0 -%}{%- assign show_tags = true -%}{%- endif -%}
          <div class="gift-flavours" data-gift-group-panel="{{ group_key }}" hidden>
            {%- assign subsets = 'adult,kids' | split: ',' -%}
            {%- for subset in subsets -%}
              {%- assign row_count = adult_count -%}
              {%- if subset == 'kids' -%}{%- assign row_count = kids_count -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- if row_count == 0 -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
              <div class="gift-flavours__row">
                {%- if show_tags -%}
                  <span class="gift-flavours__tag">{% if subset == 'kids' %}Kids{% else %}Adults{% endif %}</span>
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- for g in gift_products -%}
                  {%- unless g.available -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endunless -%}
                  {%- assign gl = g.type -%}
                  {%- if g.type contains 'Lip' -%}{%- assign gl = 'Lip Balm' -%}{%- endif -%}
                  {%- unless gl == group -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endunless -%}
                  {%- assign is_kids = false -%}
                  {%- if g.title contains 'Kids' -%}{%- assign is_kids = true -%}{%- endif -%}
                  {%- if subset == 'kids' and is_kids == false -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
                  {%- if subset == 'adult' and is_kids -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
                  {%- comment -%}
                    Drop only the words the row tag and the chip already said.
                    The scent name itself is never cut - see the note at the
                    top of this file about "Bergamot & Lemon".
                  {%- endcomment -%}
                  {%- assign flavour = g.title | remove: 'INCIA ' | remove: 'Kids Lip Balm ' | remove: 'Lip Balm ' | split: '|' | first | strip -%}
                  <button type="button" class="gift-flavour" data-add-gift data-variant-id="{{ g.selected_or_first_available_variant.id }}" data-gift-label="{{ g.title | remove: 'INCIA ' | escape }}" {% if g.tags contains 'Personalised' %}data-needs-name="Name"{% endif %} aria-label="Add free {{ g.title | remove: 'INCIA ' | escape }}">{{ flavour }}</button>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </div>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}

      <p class="gift-progress__note">One offer per order - the free gift cannot be used together with a discount code.</p>

      <div class="gift-name" data-gift-name hidden>
        <label class="gift-name__label">
          <span class="gift-name__labeltext">Baby&rsquo;s name for personalisation <span class="gift-name__req">required</span></span>
          <input type="text" maxlength="12" autocomplete="off" placeholder="e.g. Amelia" data-gift-name-input>
        </label>
        <p class="gift-name__help">Up to 12 characters. Letters, spaces, apostrophes and hyphens only. Please double check the spelling, personalised items are made to order and cannot be returned unless faulty.</p>
        <p class="gift-name__error" data-gift-name-error hidden></p>
        <div class="gift-name__actions">
          <button type="button" class="gift-name__confirm" data-gift-name-confirm>Add my free gift</button>
          <button type="button" class="gift-name__cancel" data-gift-name-cancel>Cancel</button>
        </div>
      </div>

    {%- elsif paid_gift_item -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        They already have a lip balm or the towel in the bag at full price and
        the cart may well read over £25, so "add more" looks wrong until we say
        what the £25 is actually counted on.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <p class="gift-progress__note">Lip balms and the towel do not count towards the {{ gift_threshold | money_without_trailing_zeros }} - your free gift has to be an extra item.</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
</div>
